IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qira-dates`

-- Industrial Relations Act 2016 (Qld) -- the provisions an employee bringing a claim meets: notice of termination and
-- redundancy pay (ch 2 pt 2 div 13, ss 120-127), the general protections application and its time limits (ss 309-310),
-- dismissals (ch 8 pt 2, ss 315-335), paying and recovering wages (ss 373, 376, 378-379), recovering superannuation
-- contributions (s 396) and the commission's unpaid wages jurisdiction (ss 475-477).
--
-- The core is seat-neutral: it is written in the Act's own actors ("the employee", "the employer", "the commission",
-- "the registrar"). The employee's questions are asked in qira-seat.l4, which builds these records from plain answers.
-- Judgments the Act hands to the commission or a magistrate are inputs, answered conditionally ("if the commission
-- considers ...").
--
-- Edition: act-2016-063, current in-force version on 22 September 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2016-063.txt.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Industrial Relations Act 2016 -- claims an employee meets`

§§ `The employment`

-- How the employee was engaged. The Act's words: "a casual employee", "an employee engaged by the hour or day", "an
-- employee engaged for a specific period or task" (ss 120(c), 315(1)(d), 315(4)(c)); "an employee employed for a fixed
-- period, for a fixed task, or for the duration of a particular season" (s 125(3)(c)). READING: a fixed period or task
-- is a specific period or task, and the duration of a season is a specific period (NOTES.md, fork F1).
DECLARE `Basis of engagement` IS ONE OF
    `engaged on an ongoing basis`
    `engaged as a casual employee`
    `engaged by the hour or day`
    `engaged for a specific period or task`
    `engaged for the duration of a particular season`

-- What the employee and employer agreed in writing about probation (ss 120(d)-(e), 315(1)(a)-(b), 315(4)(d)-(e)).
DECLARE `Probation agreement` IS ONE OF
    `no written agreement about probation`
    `a written agreement to serve a shorter probation than 3 months`
    `a written agreement to serve no probation`
    `a written agreement made before the employment started to serve a longer probation than 3 months`

-- One employment, ended by one dismissal (the text's natural unit).
DECLARE `The employment` HAS
    `the day continuous service started`                   IS A DATE    -- counting service with a former employer that s 132 makes service with this one (s 315(3))
    `the day the dismissal takes effect`                   IS A DATE
    `the employee's date of birth`                         IS A DATE
    `the basis of engagement`                              IS A `Basis of engagement`
    `the probation agreement`                              IS A `Probation agreement`
    `the agreed probation in months`                       IS A NUMBER  -- read only for a longer probation
    `the longer probation is a reasonable period`          IS A BOOLEAN -- a judgment on the nature and circumstances of the employment
    `engaged regularly and systematically`                 IS A BOOLEAN -- s 315(9)(a)(i)
    `engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`   IS A BOOLEAN -- s 315(9)(a)(ii)
    `had a reasonable expectation of further employment`   IS A BOOLEAN -- s 315(9)(b)
    `the main purpose of the fixed engagement was to avoid division 2` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 315(1)(d)(i), a judgment
    `in a labour market program`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 315(1)(d)(ii)
    `employed under an industrial instrument`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a public service officer employed on tenure`          IS A BOOLEAN -- under the Public Sector Act 2022
    `annual wages immediately before the dismissal`        IS A NUMBER  -- Australian dollars a year
    `the high income threshold`                            IS A NUMBER  -- Fair Work Act 2009 (Cwlth) s 333, dollars a year, a borrowed figure

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is casual` `e` IF
    CONSIDER `e`'s `the basis of engagement`
    WHEN `engaged as a casual employee` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is engaged by the hour or day` `e` IF
    CONSIDER `e`'s `the basis of engagement`
    WHEN `engaged by the hour or day` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Fork F1: a season counts as a specific period.
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is engaged for a specific period or task` `e` IF
    CONSIDER `e`'s `the basis of engagement`
    WHEN `engaged for a specific period or task` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `engaged for the duration of a particular season` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 315(1)(a), 315(4)(d), 120(d): "an employee during the first 3 months of employment with an employer (the
-- probationary period), unless the employee and employer agree in writing that the employee serve-- (i) a period of
-- probation that is shorter than the probationary period; or (ii) no period of probation".
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dismissal is in the first 3 months of employment` `e` IF
    (`e`'s `the day the dismissal takes effect`) `is before` (`the day that is` 3 `months after` (`e`'s `the day continuous service started`))

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a shorter probation or none was agreed in writing` `e` IF
    CONSIDER `e`'s `the probation agreement`
    WHEN `a written agreement to serve a shorter probation than 3 months` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a written agreement to serve no probation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the probationary period excludes the employee` `e` IF
        `the dismissal is in the first 3 months of employment` `e`
    AND (NOT (`a shorter probation or none was agreed in writing` `e`))

-- s 315(1)(b), 315(4)(e), 120(e): "an employee serving a period of probation that is longer than the probationary
-- period, if the period decided, by written agreement between the employee and employer before the employment
-- started, is a reasonable period having regard to the nature and circumstances of the employment".
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a longer probation was agreed before the employment started` `e` IF
    CONSIDER `e`'s `the probation agreement`
    WHEN `a written agreement made before the employment started to serve a longer probation than 3 months` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reasonable longer probation excludes the employee` `e` IF
        `a longer probation was agreed before the employment started` `e`
    AND `e`'s `the longer probation is a reasonable period`
    AND ((`e`'s `the day the dismissal takes effect`) `is before` (`the day that is` (`e`'s `the agreed probation in months`) `months after` (`e`'s `the day continuous service started`)))

-- s 315(9): "short term casual employee means a casual employee, other than a casual employee who-- (a) is engaged--
-- (i) by a particular employer on a regular and systematic basis; and (ii) for several periods of employment during a
-- period of at least 6 months; and (b) apart from the employer's decision not to offer the person further employment,
-- had a reasonable expectation of further employment by the employer."
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is a short term casual employee` `e` IF
        `the employee is casual` `e`
    AND (NOT (    `e`'s `engaged regularly and systematically`
              AND `e`'s `engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`
              AND `e`'s `had a reasonable expectation of further employment`))

-- s 315(1)(d): "an employee engaged for a specific period or task, unless-- (i) the main purpose of engaging the
-- employee in that way is, or was at the time of the employee's engagement, to avoid the employer's obligations under
-- division 2; or (ii) the employee is participating in a labour market program and is dismissed before the period
-- ends or the task is complete".
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specific period or task excludes the employee from unfair dismissal` `e` IF
        `the employee is engaged for a specific period or task` `e`
    AND (NOT (    `e`'s `the main purpose of the fixed engagement was to avoid division 2`
              OR (`e`'s `in a labour market program` AND `e`'s `dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete`)))

-- s 315(1)(e), 315(4)(f), 120(f): not employed under an industrial instrument, not a public service officer employed on
-- tenure, and "annual wages immediately before the dismissal are equal to or more than" the high income threshold.
-- s 120(f)(i) says "to whom an applicable industrial instrument does not apply"; read as the same fact (NOTES.md).
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the high income exclusion applies` `e` IF
        (NOT (`e`'s `employed under an industrial instrument`))
    AND (NOT (`e`'s `a public service officer employed on tenure`))
    AND `e`'s `annual wages immediately before the dismissal` AT LEAST `e`'s `the high income threshold`

§§ `Unfair dismissal (ch 8 pt 2 divs 1-2, ss 315-324)`

-- s 315(1): "Section 316 does not apply to any of the following-- (a) ... (e)". A flat negative, so the answer is no
-- for an excluded employee; otherwise s 317(1) lets the application be made. A regulation may exclude further
-- employees (s 315(6)-(7)); none is deposited (NOTES.md, finding 6).
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 316 does not apply to the employee` `e` IF
        `the probationary period excludes the employee` `e`
    OR  `a reasonable longer probation excludes the employee` `e`
    OR  `the employee is a short term casual employee` `e`
    OR  `the specific period or task excludes the employee from unfair dismissal` `e`
    OR  `the high income exclusion applies` `e`

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee may claim unfair dismissal` `e` IF
    NOT (`section 316 does not apply to the employee` `e`)

-- s 317(2): "The application must be made within-- (a) 21 days after the dismissal takes effect; or (b) if the
-- commission allows a further period on an application made at any time--the further period."
GIVEN `the day the dismissal took effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for reinstatement` `the day the dismissal took effect` MEANS
    `the day that is` 21 `days after` `the day the dismissal took effect`

-- s 317(6): "The applicant may, by written notice given within 21 days after the registrar's notice is received,
-- inform the registrar that the applicant wishes the application to proceed."
GIVEN `the day the rejection notice was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to insist that a rejected application proceed` `the day the rejection notice was received` MEANS
    `the day that is` 21 `days after` `the day the rejection notice was received`

-- s 318(4): "The application lapses if the applicant has not, within 6 months after the applicant has been informed by
-- the commission under subsection (3)-- (a) taken any action in relation to the application; or (b) discontinued the
-- application."
GIVEN `the day the commission informed the applicant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to act on the application after the certificate` `the day the commission informed the applicant` MEANS
    `the day that is` 6 `months after` `the day the commission informed the applicant`

GIVEN `the day the commission informed the applicant` IS A DATE
      `action was taken`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day action was first taken`                IS A DATE
      `the day asked about`                           IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application has lapsed` IF
        (`the last day to act on the application after the certificate` `the day the commission informed the applicant`) `is before` `the day asked about`
    AND (    (NOT `action was taken`)
         OR  ((`the last day to act on the application after the certificate` `the day the commission informed the applicant`) `is before` `the day action was first taken`))

-- s 320(1)-(2): what the commission must consider, and when it may decide a dismissal was not harsh, unjust or
-- unreasonable. The weighing is the commission's; only the list of matters is worked out here.
DECLARE `What the dismissal related to` IS ONE OF
    `the operational requirements of the employer`
    `the employee's conduct, capacity or performance`
    `something else`

DECLARE `Matter the commission considers` IS ONE OF
    `whether the employee was notified of the reason for dismissal`
    `whether the dismissal related to operational requirements or to conduct, capacity or performance`
    `whether the employee had been warned about the conduct, capacity or performance`
    `whether the employee was given an opportunity to respond`
    `any other matters the commission considers relevant`
    `the commission may decide the dismissal was not harsh, unjust or unreasonable because the conduct at work was unlawful or harassment`

GIVEN `related to`                         IS A `What the dismissal related to`
      `the conduct was at work or connected with the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct was unlawful or sexual or sex or gender-based harassment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Matter the commission considers`
`the matters the commission must consider` `related to` `the conduct was at work or connected with the employment` `the conduct was unlawful or sexual or sex or gender-based harassment` MEANS
    IF `about conduct`
    THEN IF `the conduct was at work or connected with the employment` AND `the conduct was unlawful or sexual or sex or gender-based harassment`
         THEN LIST `whether the employee was notified of the reason for dismissal`, `whether the dismissal related to operational requirements or to conduct, capacity or performance`, `whether the employee had been warned about the conduct, capacity or performance`, `whether the employee was given an opportunity to respond`, `any other matters the commission considers relevant`, `the commission may decide the dismissal was not harsh, unjust or unreasonable because the conduct at work was unlawful or harassment`
         ELSE LIST `whether the employee was notified of the reason for dismissal`, `whether the dismissal related to operational requirements or to conduct, capacity or performance`, `whether the employee had been warned about the conduct, capacity or performance`, `whether the employee was given an opportunity to respond`, `any other matters the commission considers relevant`
    ELSE LIST `whether the employee was notified of the reason for dismissal`, `whether the dismissal related to operational requirements or to conduct, capacity or performance`, `any other matters the commission considers relevant`
    WHERE
        `about conduct` MEANS
            CONSIDER `related to`
            WHEN `the employee's conduct, capacity or performance` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 322(1): "If, and only if, the commission considers reinstatement or re-employment would be impracticable, the
-- commission may order the employer to pay the employee an amount of compensation". (2) the cap: "(a) if the employee
-- was employed under an industrial instrument--the wages the employer would have been liable to pay the employee for
-- the 6 months immediately after the dismissal, paid at the rate the employee received immediately before the
-- dismissal; or (b) if the employee was not employed under an industrial instrument--the lesser of the wages under
-- paragraph (a) and an amount equal to half the amount of the high income threshold". READING: 6 months' wages at the
-- rate before the dismissal is half the annual wages at that rate (NOTES.md, finding 9).
DECLARE `Compensation answer` IS ONE OF
    `the commission may award compensation of no more than` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no compensation can be ordered, because the commission does not consider reinstatement or re-employment impracticable`

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 322(2) cap` `e` MEANS
    IF `e`'s `employed under an industrial instrument`
    THEN `six months wages`
    ELSE `the lesser of` `six months wages` `and` (`e`'s `the high income threshold` DIVIDED BY 2)
    WHERE
        `six months wages` MEANS `e`'s `annual wages immediately before the dismissal` DIVIDED BY 2

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
      `the commission considers reinstatement impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Compensation answer`
`the most unfair dismissal compensation` `e` `the commission considers reinstatement impracticable` MEANS
    IF `the commission considers reinstatement impracticable`
    THEN `the commission may award compensation of no more than` (`the s 322(2) cap` `e`)
    ELSE `no compensation can be ordered, because the commission does not consider reinstatement or re-employment impracticable`

-- s 323(1)(a): if the employer wilfully contravenes an order to reinstate or re-employ, a further order to pay "(i) an
-- amount of not more than the monetary value of 50 penalty units; and (ii) an amount for lost wages". The value of a
-- penalty unit is set under the Penalties and Sentences Act 1992, not deposited: an input.
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most extra amount for a wilful failure to reinstate` `the value of a penalty unit` MEANS
    50 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`

§§ `Requirements for dismissal (ch 8 pt 2 div 3, ss 325-331)`

-- s 315(4): "Division 3 does not apply to-- (a) a casual employee; or (b) an employee engaged by the hour or day; (c) an
-- employee engaged for a specific period or task; or (d) [the probationary period] ... (e) [a reasonable longer
-- probation] ... (f) [high income]". (5): "Division 3 does not apply to an employee with less than 1 year of
-- continuous service." (8): "Divisions 3 to 5 do not apply to an employee participating in a labour market program."
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `division 3 does not apply to the employee` `e` IF
        `the employee is casual` `e`
    OR  `the employee is engaged by the hour or day` `e`
    OR  `the employee is engaged for a specific period or task` `e`
    OR  `the probationary period excludes the employee` `e`
    OR  `a reasonable longer probation excludes the employee` `e`
    OR  `the high income exclusion applies` `e`
    OR  (NOT (`service from` (`e`'s `the day continuous service started`) `is at least` 1 `years on` (`e`'s `the day the dismissal takes effect`)))
    OR  `e`'s `in a labour market program`

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `division 3 protects the employee` `e` IF
    NOT (`division 3 does not apply to the employee` `e`)

-- ss 327, 331: "An application for an order under this subdivision must be made-- (a) before, or within 21 days after,
-- the dismissal takes effect; or (b) within a further period the commission allows".
GIVEN `the day the dismissal took effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply about severance or a mass dismissal` `the day the dismissal took effect` MEANS
    `the day that is` 21 `days after` `the day the dismissal took effect`

-- s 328: "This subdivision applies if an employer decides to dismiss 15 or more employees for an economic,
-- technological or structural reason." Then ss 329 (notify Centrelink's agency and each union) and 330 (consult).
GIVEN `the number of employees the employer decided to dismiss` IS A NUMBER
      `for an economic, technological or structural reason`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subdivision 2 applies to the decision` IF
        `the number of employees the employer decided to dismiss` AT LEAST 15
    AND `for an economic, technological or structural reason`

-- s 326(3)(b): "an amount of not more than the monetary value of 135 penalty units"; s 329(3)(c) the same; s 329(3)(b)
-- a penalty of "not more than 16 penalty units", which s 329(5) lets the commission order paid to the applicant.
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the employer can be ordered to pay the employee under ss 326 or 329` `the value of a penalty unit` MEANS
    135 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`

GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most penalty under s 329(3)(b)` `the value of a penalty unit` MEANS
    16 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`

§§ `Stand-down (ch 8 pt 2 div 4, ss 332-333)`

DECLARE `Christmas public holiday` IS ONE OF
    `Christmas Eve, from 6pm to midnight`
    `Christmas Day`
    `Boxing Day`
    `New Year's Day`

-- s 332(1): "an employee, other than a casual employee, who-- (a) is stood down by an employer during December; and
-- (b) is re-employed by the employer before the end of the next January; and (c) was employed by the employer for a
-- continuous period of at least 2 weeks immediately before being stood down." (3): "stand-down includes dismissal".
-- s 315(8): not for an employee in a labour market program.
GIVEN `the employee is a casual employee`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a labour market program`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the continuous period started`   IS A DATE
      `the day of the stand-down`               IS A DATE
      `the day of re-employment`                IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 332 applies` IF
        (NOT `the employee is a casual employee`)
    AND (NOT `in a labour market program`)
    AND DATE_MONTH `the day of the stand-down` EQUALS 12
    AND (`the day of re-employment` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 ((DATE_YEAR `the day of the stand-down`) PLUS 1)))
    AND ((`the day that is` 14 `days after` `the day the continuous period started`) `is on or before` `the day of the stand-down`)

-- s 332(2): the employer "must pay the employee at the ordinary rate ... for the Christmas Eve (from 6p.m. to midnight),
-- Christmas Day, Boxing Day, and New Year's Day public holidays between the stand-down and the re-employment." READING:
-- a holiday is between them if it falls on or after the day of the stand-down and before the day of re-employment
-- (NOTES.md, fork F3). The days are the calendar days the section names; substituted holidays are not read.
GIVEN `the employee is a casual employee`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a labour market program`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the continuous period started`   IS A DATE
      `the day of the stand-down`               IS A DATE
      `the day of re-employment`                IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Christmas public holiday`
`the stand-down public holidays the employer must pay` `the employee is a casual employee` `in a labour market program` `the day the continuous period started` `the day of the stand-down` `the day of re-employment` MEANS
    IF `section 332 applies` `the employee is a casual employee` `in a labour market program` `the day the continuous period started` `the day of the stand-down` `the day of re-employment`
    THEN filter (GIVEN h YIELD `is between` h) (LIST `Christmas Eve, from 6pm to midnight`, `Christmas Day`, `Boxing Day`, `New Year's Day`)
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        `the year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day of the stand-down`
        GIVEN h IS A `Christmas public holiday`
        GIVETH A DATE
        `the day of` h MEANS
            CONSIDER h
            WHEN `Christmas Eve, from 6pm to midnight` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 24 12 `the year`
            WHEN `Christmas Day` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 25 12 `the year`
            WHEN `Boxing Day` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 26 12 `the year`
            WHEN `New Year's Day` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 (`the year` PLUS 1)
        GIVEN h IS A `Christmas public holiday`
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `is between` h MEANS
                `the day of the stand-down` `is on or before` (`the day of` h)
            AND ((`the day of` h) `is before` `the day of re-employment`)

-- s 333: "(1) An employer may stand down an employee on a day, or for part of a day, when the employee can not be
-- usefully employed because of something that happened-- (a) for which the employer is not responsible; or (b) over
-- which the employer has no control. (2) The employer may stand down the employee without pay, unless an industrial
-- instrument provides otherwise." JUST TRUE where s 333 gives the permission; JUST FALSE where the instrument provides
-- otherwise ("unless"); NOTHING where the case is outside the grant (s 333 is silent; scope limit, ruling (c)).
GIVEN `the employee can not be usefully employed`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause is something the employer is not responsible for or has no control over` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an industrial instrument provides otherwise`                  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333 lets the employer stand the employee down without pay` `the employee can not be usefully employed` `the cause is something the employer is not responsible for or has no control over` `an industrial instrument provides otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the employee can not be usefully employed` AND `the cause is something the employer is not responsible for or has no control over`
    THEN IF `an industrial instrument provides otherwise`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Notice of termination (ch 2 pt 2 div 13 sdiv 1, ss 120-124)`

-- s 120: "This subdivision does not apply to any of the following-- (a) a casual employee; (b) an employee engaged by
-- the hour or day; (c) an employee engaged for a specific period or task; (d) [the probationary period] ... (e) [a
-- reasonable longer probation] ... (f) [high income] ... (g) an employee participating in a labour market program."
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice subdivision does not apply to the employee` `e` IF
        `the employee is casual` `e`
    OR  `the employee is engaged by the hour or day` `e`
    OR  `the employee is engaged for a specific period or task` `e`
    OR  `the probationary period excludes the employee` `e`
    OR  `a reasonable longer probation excludes the employee` `e`
    OR  `the high income exclusion applies` `e`
    OR  `e`'s `in a labour market program`

-- s 123(1): "(a) if the employee's continuous service is-- (i) not more than 1 year--1 week; and (ii) more than 1 year,
-- but not more than 3 years--2 weeks; and (iii) more than 3 years, but not more than 5 years--3 weeks; and (iv) more
-- than 5 years--4 weeks; and (b) increased by 1 week if the employee-- (i) is 45 years of age or over; and (ii) has
-- completed at least 2 years of continuous service with the employer." Service and age are taken on the day the
-- dismissal takes effect (NOTES.md, finding 11).
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum weeks of notice` `e` MEANS
    `the s 123(1)(a) weeks` PLUS `the s 123(1)(b) week`
    WHERE
        `started` MEANS `e`'s `the day continuous service started`
        `ends`    MEANS `e`'s `the day the dismissal takes effect`
        `the s 123(1)(a) weeks` MEANS
            BRANCH IF (`service from` `started` `is more than` 5 `years on` `ends`) THEN 4
                   IF (`service from` `started` `is more than` 3 `years on` `ends`) THEN 3
                   IF (`service from` `started` `is more than` 1 `years on` `ends`) THEN 2
                   OTHERWISE 1
        `the s 123(1)(b) week` MEANS
            IF     `someone born on` (`e`'s `the employee's date of birth`) `is at least` 45 `on` `ends`
               AND (`service from` `started` `is at least` 2 `years on` `ends`)
            THEN 1
            ELSE 0

DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `the minimum notice, in weeks, is` HAS `weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `the notice subdivision does not apply to me (s 120)`

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`the notice the employer must give` `e` MEANS
    IF `the notice subdivision does not apply to the employee` `e`
    THEN `the notice subdivision does not apply to me (s 120)`
    ELSE `the minimum notice, in weeks, is` (`the minimum weeks of notice` `e`)

-- s 124(1)-(2): compensation "at least equal to the total of the amounts the employer would have been liable to pay the
-- employee if the employee's employment had continued until the end of the required notice period", worked out on the
-- ordinary working hours and the amounts payable for them (allowances, loadings, penalties) and other contract amounts.
-- The weekly total is the employee's figure.
DECLARE `Pay in lieu answer` IS ONE OF
    `the minimum compensation instead of notice, in Australian dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the notice subdivision does not apply to me (s 120) so s 124 sets no minimum`

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
      `the weekly amount for ordinary hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pay in lieu answer`
`the minimum compensation instead of notice` `e` `the weekly amount for ordinary hours` MEANS
    IF `the notice subdivision does not apply to the employee` `e`
    THEN `the notice subdivision does not apply to me (s 120) so s 124 sets no minimum`
    ELSE `the minimum compensation instead of notice, in Australian dollars, is` ((`the minimum weeks of notice` `e`) TIMES `the weekly amount for ordinary hours`)

-- s 121(1)(b)-(3): dismissal without notice or compensation for "misconduct of a type that would make it unreasonable
-- to require the employer to continue the employment during the period of notice"; (2) "misconduct includes ...
-- theft; assault; sexual harassment or sex or gender based-harassment; fraud; other misconduct prescribed by
-- regulation"; (3) "subsection (1)(b) does not apply if the employee can show that, in the circumstances, the conduct
-- was not conduct that made it unreasonable to continue the employment during the period of notice."
-- READING (fork F2): a listed kind is taken as misconduct of that type unless the employee shows otherwise; other
-- conduct is left to the "includes" list (NOTHING); no misconduct at all is the text's "only if" (JUST FALSE).
DECLARE `Kind of conduct` IS ONE OF
    `theft`
    `assault`
    `sexual harassment or sex or gender based harassment`
    `fraud`
    `other misconduct prescribed by regulation`
    `other conduct the employer calls misconduct`
    `no misconduct`

GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
      `the conduct` IS A `Kind of conduct`
      `the employee can show the conduct did not make continuing unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer may dismiss without notice or compensation` `e` `the conduct` `the employee can show the conduct did not make continuing unreasonable` MEANS
    IF `the notice subdivision does not apply to the employee` `e`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the conduct`
         WHEN `no misconduct` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `other conduct the employer calls misconduct` THEN
             IF `the employee can show the conduct did not make continuing unreasonable` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
         OTHERWISE
             IF `the employee can show the conduct did not make continuing unreasonable` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 122(3): an application for an order for the compensation "must be made within 6 years after the day on which the
-- employee is dismissed."
GIVEN `the day of dismissal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to claim notice compensation` `the day of dismissal` MEANS
    `the day that is` 6 `years after` `the day of dismissal`

§§ `Redundancy pay (ch 2 pt 2 div 13 sdiv 2, ss 125-127)`

DECLARE `The redundancy` HAS
    `the employer no longer requires the job done by anyone`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the termination is ordinary and customary turnover of labour`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a regulation or instrument excludes the employee`               IS A BOOLEAN -- s 125(3)(e)
    `a substantial reason for the fixed engagement was to avoid the division` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 125(4), a judgment
    `the commission ordered a reduced amount`                        IS A BOOLEAN -- s 127
    `the reduced amount ordered`                                     IS A NUMBER

-- s 125: applies if "(a) an applicable industrial instrument applies to the employee; and (b) the employee's
-- employment is terminated because the employer no longer requires the job done by the employee to be done by
-- anyone"; (2) not for "the ordinary and customary turnover of labour"; (3) not for "(a) a casual employee; (b) an
-- employee whose period of continuous service with the employer is less than 1 year; (c) an employee employed for a
-- fixed period, for a fixed task, or for the duration of a particular season; (d) an employee participating in a
-- labour market program; (e) another employee prescribed"; (4) "(c) does not prevent this subdivision applying ... if a
-- substantial reason for employing the employee as mentioned in the subsection was to avoid the application of this
-- division."
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
      `r` IS A `The redundancy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the redundancy subdivision applies` `e` `r` IF
        `e`'s `employed under an industrial instrument`
    AND `r`'s `the employer no longer requires the job done by anyone`
    AND (NOT (`r`'s `the termination is ordinary and customary turnover of labour`))
    AND (NOT (`the employee is casual` `e`))
    AND (`service from` (`e`'s `the day continuous service started`) `is at least` 1 `years on` (`e`'s `the day the dismissal takes effect`))
    AND (NOT (`the employee is engaged for a specific period or task` `e` AND (NOT (`r`'s `a substantial reason for the fixed engagement was to avoid the division`))))
    AND (NOT (`e`'s `in a labour market program`))
    AND (NOT (`r`'s `a regulation or instrument excludes the employee`))

-- s 126(1) table: "at least 1 year but not more than 2 years--4 weeks; more than 2 years but not more than 3 years--6
-- weeks; ... more than 11 years but not more than 12 years--15 weeks; more than 12 years--16 weeks".
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the redundancy pay period in weeks` `e` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `more than` 12 THEN 16
           IF `more than` 11 THEN 15
           IF `more than` 10 THEN 14
           IF `more than` 9  THEN 13
           IF `more than` 8  THEN 12
           IF `more than` 7  THEN 11
           IF `more than` 6  THEN 10
           IF `more than` 5  THEN 9
           IF `more than` 4  THEN 8
           IF `more than` 3  THEN 7
           IF `more than` 2  THEN 6
           IF (`service from` (`e`'s `the day continuous service started`) `is at least` 1 `years on` (`e`'s `the day the dismissal takes effect`)) THEN 4
           OTHERWISE 0
    WHERE
        GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `more than` `n` MEANS `service from` (`e`'s `the day continuous service started`) `is more than` `n` `years on` (`e`'s `the day the dismissal takes effect`)

DECLARE `Redundancy answer` IS ONE OF
    `my redundancy pay, in Australian dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the redundancy pay subdivision does not apply to me (s 125)`

-- s 126(1)-(2): redundancy pay is "the total amount payable to the employee for the redundancy pay period", "worked out
-- on the basis of the employee's weeks pay for the employee's ordinary hours of work"; s 127(4): where the commission
-- orders a reduced amount (which may be zero), the entitlement "is the amount stated in the order".
GIVEN `e` IS A `The employment`
      `r` IS A `The redundancy`
      `a week's pay for ordinary hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Redundancy answer`
`the redundancy pay` `e` `r` `a week's pay for ordinary hours` MEANS
    IF `the redundancy subdivision applies` `e` `r`
    THEN IF `r`'s `the commission ordered a reduced amount`
         THEN `my redundancy pay, in Australian dollars, is` (`r`'s `the reduced amount ordered`)
         ELSE `my redundancy pay, in Australian dollars, is` ((`the redundancy pay period in weeks` `e`) TIMES `a week's pay for ordinary hours`)
    ELSE `the redundancy pay subdivision does not apply to me (s 125)`

§§ `General protections applications (ch 8 pt 1 div 8, ss 309-310)`

-- s 310(1): an application relating to dismissal "must be made within-- (a) 21 days after the dismissal took effect; or
-- (b) if the commission allows a further period under subsection (2)--the further period" (exceptional circumstances).
-- (3): "An application relating to a contravention of this part (other than dismissal) must be made within 6 years
-- after the contravention occurs."
GIVEN `the day the dismissal took effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply about a dismissal under the general protections` `the day the dismissal took effect` MEANS
    `the day that is` 21 `days after` `the day the dismissal took effect`

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply about another general protections contravention` `the day of the contravention` MEANS
    `the day that is` 6 `years after` `the day of the contravention`

§§ `Wages and superannuation (ss 373, 376, 378-379, 396, 475-477)`

-- ss 379(3), 396(3), 476(4): the application "must be made within 6 years after the amount claimed became payable";
-- ss 379(4)(a), 396(4)(a), 475(1), 477(1)(a)(i): the order is for amounts payable and unpaid "within the 6 years before
-- the date of the application". READING: the two say the same thing, so an amount is recoverable if the application
-- is made on or before the sixth anniversary of the day it became payable (NOTES.md, finding 13).
GIVEN `the day the amount became payable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for an unpaid amount` `the day the amount became payable` MEANS
    `the day that is` 6 `years after` `the day the amount became payable`

GIVEN `the day the amount became payable` IS A DATE
      `the day of the application`        IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unpaid amount can still be ordered` IF
    `the day of the application` `is on or before` (`the last day to apply for an unpaid amount` `the day the amount became payable`)

-- Where an unpaid wages claim may go. s 379: a magistrate, but s 379(5) "A person can not make an application under
-- this section if an application has been made under section 475 or 396 for the same matter." s 476(1): the commission
-- "only if the total amount claimed is $100,000 or less"; (3) not "if an application has been made under section 379,
-- 386 or 396 for the same matter". s 386 (clothing outworkers) is out of scope, so a s 386 application is not asked.
DECLARE `Forum for unpaid wages` IS ONE OF
    `a magistrate (s 379)`
    `the commission (ss 475-476)`

GIVEN `the total amount claimed`                          IS A NUMBER
      `already applied to a magistrate under s 379`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `already applied to the commission under s 475`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `already applied to a magistrate under s 396`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Forum for unpaid wages`
`where an unpaid wages claim can be made` `the total amount claimed` `already applied to a magistrate under s 379` `already applied to the commission under s 475` `already applied to a magistrate under s 396` MEANS
    IF `magistrate open`
    THEN IF `commission open` THEN LIST `a magistrate (s 379)`, `the commission (ss 475-476)` ELSE LIST `a magistrate (s 379)`
    ELSE IF `commission open` THEN LIST `the commission (ss 475-476)` ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        `magistrate open` MEANS
            NOT (`already applied to the commission under s 475` OR `already applied to a magistrate under s 396`)
        `commission open` MEANS
                `the total amount claimed` AT MOST 100000
            AND (NOT (`already applied to a magistrate under s 379` OR `already applied to a magistrate under s 396`))

-- s 376(2)-(3): the employer "may recover an amount to which the employee is not entitled by deducting amounts from the
-- employee's wages for a subsequent pay period or periods"; deductions "(a) must start within 1 year after the
-- payment; and (b) may extend over a period of 6 years after the payment." A fixed period, so outside it the answer is
-- no (periods ruling (a)). s 376(4) (the regulation's floor) is not deposited.
GIVEN `the day of the overpayment`         IS A DATE
      `the day deductions started`         IS A DATE
      `the day of this deduction`          IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer may deduct the overpayment from these wages` IF
        `the day of the overpayment` `is before` `the day deductions started`
    AND (`the day deductions started` `is on or before` (`the day that is` 1 `years after` `the day of the overpayment`))
    AND (`the day deductions started` `is on or before` `the day of this deduction`)
    AND (`the day of this deduction` `is on or before` (`the day that is` 6 `years after` `the day of the overpayment`))

§§ `Regulative rules`

DECLARE `IR party` IS ONE OF
    `the employee`
    `the employer`
    `the commission`

DECLARE `IR act` IS ONE OF
    `apply for reinstatement`
    `apply for a further period`
    `inform the registrar the application is to proceed`
    `deal with the application`
    `apply to the commission to deal with the dismissal dispute`
    `pay the wages`

-- s 317(2): applying is the employee's choice (s 317(1) "may be made"), so a late application is no breach: the
-- employee may then ask for a further period, which s 317(2)(b) lets the commission allow "on an application made at
-- any time". Day 0 is the day the dismissal takes effect; the window is 21 days.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `IR party` `IR act`
DECIDE `s 317 -- the employee may apply for reinstatement within 21 days, and after that ask for a further period` IS
    PARTY `the employee`
    DO    `apply for reinstatement`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY `the employee` MAY `apply for a further period`)

-- s 317(6)-(7): "The applicant may, by written notice given within 21 days after the registrar's notice is received,
-- inform the registrar that the applicant wishes the application to proceed. If the applicant does so, the commission
-- must deal with the application, despite the registrar's rejection." Day 0 is the day the registrar's notice is
-- received. Not insisting is no breach: the rejection stands.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `IR party` `IR act`
DECIDE `s 317(6)-(7) -- after a rejection, insisting within 21 days obliges the commission to deal with the application` IS
    PARTY `the employee`
    DO    `inform the registrar the application is to proceed`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE (PARTY `the commission` MUST `deal with the application`)
    LEST  FULFILLED

-- s 310(1)-(2): the general protections application about a dismissal, 21 days, then a further period only on
-- exceptional circumstances (the commission's judgment).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `IR party` `IR act`
DECIDE `s 310 -- the employee may apply about a dismissal within 21 days, and after that ask for a further period` IS
    PARTY `the employee`
    DO    `apply to the commission to deal with the dismissal dispute`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY `the employee` MAY `apply for a further period`)

-- s 373(1): "An employer must pay each employee's wages at least monthly to the employee. Maximum penalty--16 penalty
-- units." Day 0 is the day after the last payment; the window is the number of days to the same day next month.
GIVEN `days to the same day next month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `IR party` `IR act`
DECIDE `s 373 -- the employer must pay the wages at least monthly` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the wages`
    WITHIN `days to the same day next month`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 373(1): an employer must pay each employee's wages at least monthly (maximum penalty 16 penalty units)"
